// Teams and model tiers (vault designs/teams-and-tiers-2026-11-10.md), the owner's install (10 Nov, m312-m329). coordd
// asks these acts; an act left out is not checked.

// The order of models within a family: a subagent runs a lower tier than the agent that starts it.
Fact tier Identified by model * Int
+tier("claude-haiku-5-5", 1).
+tier("claude-sonnet-5-5", 2).
+tier("claude-sonnet-5", 2).
+tier("claude-opus-5-5", 3).
+tier("claude-opus-5", 3).
+tier("claude-fable-5-1", 4).
+tier("claude-fable-5-2", 4).
+tier("gpt-6-luna", 1).
+tier("gpt-6-astra", 2).

// Claude Code's Agent tool (the PreToolUse hook): within the agent's family and a lower tier; another family is a
// team's job. A call naming no model runs the agent's own model, so it is refused here.
Act start-subagent
  Actor agent
  Related to model
  Holds when family(model) == family(runs(actor)) and tier(model) < tier(runs(actor))

// `coord team ask`: any agent but a team member (depth: owner, orch, its agents, an agent's team).
Act ask-team
  Actor agent
  Holds when not member(actor)

// Who an ask goes to and who may grant it: the asker's lead (its parent). The owner always may.
Act approve-team
  Actor agent
  Recipient agent
  Holds when parent(recipient, actor)

// An agent registering a new agent (roster add, roster fork): the lead staffs; others within their team grant.
Act add-agent
  Actor agent
  Holds when role(actor, "lead")
  Holds when used(actor) < granted(actor)
